{{der-bottom}}

===Etymology 2===
{{back-form|mitome|lang=en|nodot=1}}, reinforced by {{m|en|chromosome}}. Early examples include {{m|en|biome}} (1916) and {{m|en|genome}}, from {{cog|de|Genom}} (1920).<ref>{{R:OED2}}</ref> Some association with genetics due to occurrence in {{m|en|chromosome}} and {{m|en|genome}}.

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} The complete whole of a class of substances for a species or an individual.

